de\n- Addresses security concerns with AI agent implementations\n\n## How It Works\n\nAccording to coverage from **[InfoQ](https://www.infoq.com/news/2026/02/github-agentic-workflows/)** and **[DevClass](https://www.devclass.com/ci-cd/2026/02/17/github-previews-agentic-workflows-as-part-of-continuous-ai-concept/4091356)**:\n\n- **AI agents run automatically in GitHub Actions**\n- Uses Large Language Model (LLM) natural language understanding\n- Developers can define automation goals in simple Markdown files\n- Capable of handling:\n  - Issue triage\n  - Code reviews\n  - Repository maintenance\n  - CI/CD automation\n\n## GitHub Repository\n\nThe official GitHub repository for this feature is available at: **[github/gh-aw](https://github.com/github/gh-aw)**\n\nThis represents a significant shift in how developers interact with CI/CD pipelines, moving from traditional YAML configuration to natural language-based automation using AI agents.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
